Description: Home Assistant kiosk for wall-mounted displays
 HA-Panel shows the Home Assistant dashboard fullscreen on a display and
 gives a control drawer for the things a kiosk panel needs: volume, mute,
 screen power, brightness, Wi-Fi, and the audio input and output
 endpoints.
 .
 It runs on a device with a desktop session or on one with only a bare
 wlroots compositor, and it is built for a device with 2 GB of RAM and
 4 GB of storage. Logs are kept in memory and only reach the disk when
 something fails.
